    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d924">

                <pb facs="1432" n="1418" xml:id="pg1418"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 E.W./9–644: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-06T16:00:00+01:00">September 6,
                            1944—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 6—3:58 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2755. ReEmbs 2703, September 1, 5 p.m.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d924-f1"/> In
                    conversation with Sampayo yesterday I again made reference to the question of
                    asylum for war criminals. Sampayo stated that note had been taken of our
                    position in this respect. He added that there was no pending request before the
                    Portuguese Government on the subject.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Norweb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
